  READ IT AGAINST MON_base, NOT AGAINST DENSE. Both moves are about
  per-block capacity, and MON_base is the arm that has neither.

  Q12 arms cost exactly the same FLOPs as MON_base, so any bpb they buy is
  free Pareto movement. Check MON_perm_random FIRST: if it moves as much as
  freq or file, coherence is not the mechanism and the result is about
  something else.

  Q13 arms cost more, so compare against the break-even in the header:
    r=16  +0.0299    r=32  +0.0289    r=64  +0.0270
  and against the equal-cost m1 (144 / 160 / 192), whose projected gain is
  0.0032 / 0.0063 / 0.0108 bpb. A residual that buys less than the m1 it
  displaces means shared directions are worth less than private ones, and
  the answer to depth 12 is simply a bigger m1.
